om the class name (`learn-skill`, `gain-ability`, `finish-random-research-project`, `install-implant`, …) so a modded comp gets its own without a hand-maintained table.\n\nACCEPTANCE BULLETS THAT CHANGED, and why\n* \"maxed skill for a trainer\" — DROPPED. Unreachable (correction 4). The two real `LearnSkill` refusals are `no-skills` and `skill-disabled`.\n* \"the item is destroyed\" — asserted PER DEF via `destroys_self`, not universally: `CompUseEffect_DestroySelf` is a comp, and no `CompUsable` building carries it.\n* \"gains the skill levels\" — restated as +50,000 XP.\n* The techprof-core bullet now says the run HALTS on a `Dialog_NodeTree` during the advance and `dialog-choose` clears it (addition J), so the halt does not read as a regression. The verb discloses it up front as `advance_halt`.","files":null}]}